2. Immune track should still allow placement of the "block on track end button" (so it remains visible/usable)
3. But it won't take effect due to the track being protected

Looking at my previous implementation, I modified the "Spin/Skip" button to be immune to ranked tracks, but the user actually wants the "block on track end button" to remain functional (visible) but not take effect on immune tracks.

Let me examine the current implementation of the "block on track end button" which is the deferred block button (handleToggleDeferredBlock).

From my previous examination, I saw this code:
```
const handleToggleDeferredBlock = () => {
  // Ranked tracks are immune to deferred block — only Block & Skip Now is allowed
  const currentRank =
    displayStats[currentTrack?.id || '']?.hazard_rank ??
    currentTrack?.hazard_rank ??
    null;
  if (currentRank !== null) {
    showToast('🛡️ Ranked tracks cannot be queued for block — use Block & Skip Now', 'warn');
    return;
  }
  // ... rest of function
}
```

And the button UI:
```
{/* Block Button 2: Deferred Block on Track End (Rating Mode) */}
<button
  type="button"
  disabled={isLogging || isExhausted || !currentTrack || isRankedImmune}
  onClick={handleToggleDeferredBlock}
  title={isRankedImmune ? '🛡️ Ranked track — use Block & Skip Now' : undefined}
  className={/* ... */}
>
  <Clock className="w-3.5 h-3.5 text-rose-400" />
  <span>
    {isRankedImmune
      ? '🛡️ Immune (Ranked)'
      : selectedScore === 'block'
      ? '✓ Queued to Block on End'
      : 'Block on Track End'}
  </span>
</button>
```

I see the issue - the button IS already disabled for ranked/immune tracks via `disabled={isLogging || isExhausted || !currentTrack || isRankedImmune}`, and it shows "🛡️ Immune (Ranked)" when immune.

But the user wants the button to REMAIN VISIBLE and ALLOW THEM TO PLACE IT (click it) even on immune tracks, but for it to NOT TAKE EFFECT (i.e., not actually queue the block).

So I need to:
1. Remove the `isRankedImmune` from the disabled attribute so the button stays clickable
2. Modify the `handleToggleDeferredBlock` function to show a toast when clicked on immune tracks instead of returning early
3. Keep the button UI showing it's immune but still allow interaction

